            <ArticleTitle>Giant cell arteritis of coronary arteries causing myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>487-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of giant cell arteritis involving the coronary arteries and causing thrombosis and myocardial infarction is described. IgM deposits in the affected arteries were demonstrated by an immunoperoxidase technique.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
